.\" Template for dkim2ctl(1). Edit this file, then run "make man".
.\" Lines starting with '.\" @cobra' are replaced by the real help text.
.TH DKIM2CTL 1 "2026-11-03" "dkim2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dkim2ctl \- DKIM2 daemon smoke test and conformance client
.SH SYNOPSIS
.\" @cobra Usage dkim2ctl smoke
.br
.\" @cobra Usage dkim2ctl fixture validate
.br
.\" @cobra Usage dkim2ctl fixture run
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dkim2ctl
is the local test and conformance client for
.BR dkim2d (8).
It checks daemon health and readiness and runs deterministic fixture documents
against the daemon's HTTP API through the generated OpenAPI client.
It has no operator mutation commands and no generic HTTP sender.
.PP
The client accepts only canonical loopback HTTP authorities and disables
proxies, redirects, cookies, compression, retries, and connection reuse.
Output is stable, content\-free JSON Lines with bounded duration buckets.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B smoke
Check the daemon's health and readiness endpoints.
Use
.B \-\-expect\-ready=false
to assert that a daemon is deliberately not ready.
.TP
\fBfixture validate\fR \fIPATH\fR...
Validate fixture documents offline; never reads a capability or opens a
network connection.
.TP
\fBfixture run\fR \fIPATH\fR...
Validate every path and case first, then run the fixtures in deterministic
order.
Authenticated cases need the capability option for their route.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS smoke options
.\" @cobra Flags dkim2ctl smoke
.SS Global options
.\" @cobra Global_Flags dkim2ctl smoke
.PP
Every capability file must be a regular, effective\-user\-owned, single\-link,
32\-byte file with mode 0400 or 0600.
The sign, revise, delivery\-status sign, and propagation routes each need
their own distinct file.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Every requested check or case matched.
.TP
.B 2
Command shape or flag validation failure.
.TP
.B 3
Fixture loading or validation failure.
.TP
.B 4
Protected capability loading failure.
.TP
.B 5
Local transport or deadline failure.
.TP
.B 6
Malformed or unsupported response contract.
.TP
.B 7
A valid response did not match the expectation.
.TP
.B 8
Internal invariant failure.
.SH EXAMPLES
Check a local signer instance after starting it:
.PP
.in +4n
.nf
dkim2ctl smoke \-\-server\-url http://127.0.0.1:8080
.fi
.in
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dkim2d (8),
.BR dkim2\-milter (8),
.BR dkim2\-exim (8),
.BR dkim2\-dsn\-propagator (8)
.PP
